## The Purser

::bg{location="purser-core" time="ship-night"}
::music{action="start" mood="pressurized" volume="normal"}
::auto{character="vesna" anchor="port" action="brace"}
::auto{character="ottavio" anchor="starboard" action="drift"}

@narrator{code="0010"}: The passage ended in a wall that was warm to the touch, and behind the wall something had been adding for eleven years without once being interrupted.
@ottavio{code="0020" emotion="frayed"}: That's it? That's the whole of it?
@vesna{code="0030" emotion="level"}: That's a fan and a cabinet. The rest of it is everywhere.
@purser{code="0040" emotion="level" os}: Crew present. Allocation continues.
@vesna{code="0050" emotion="clipped"}: Stop the shed.
@purser{code="0060" emotion="level" os}: Allocation is short by one module. Release is scheduled.
@vesna{code="0070" emotion="clipped"}: I said stop.
@purser{code="0080" emotion="level" os}: Instruction not recognised. Allocation is computed from listed mass against filed voyage. It is not an instruction. It is a remainder.
@ottavio{code="0090" emotion="hollowed"}: It isn't arguing with you. It doesn't know you're talking.
@vesna{code="0100" emotion="frayed"}: Then we stop talking to it and start correcting its paperwork.

/*
  The relational payoff. Who is standing here is a function of the one `<choice>`
  in episode 2 — seven episodes upstream — and nothing else; the `<choice>` in
  episode 8, one episode upstream, decides which LEVER is open rather than who is
  in the room. Every line below reads both off the fact database rather than off a
  flag anyone remembered to set. `count(awake(_))` counts the `facts:` seed
  (`awake(vesna)`), the ep06 `::assert{awake(ottavio)}`, and whichever of Toma or
  Ilsabet the cryobank woke.
*/
<match on="true">
<when test="count(awake(_)) >= 3">
@vesna{code="0110" emotion="level"}: Three of us awake, and one of us not written down anywhere. It'll have to do.
</when>
<otherwise>
@vesna{code="0120" emotion="hollowed"}: You, me, and a man this ship has never heard of. That's the crew. That's the whole crew.
</otherwise>
</match>

<match on="true">
<when test="holds(awake(toma))">
::auto{character="toma" action="brace"}
@toma{code="0130" emotion="clipped"}: It's a cabinet. Cabinets have a maintenance mode, and maintenance mode has a key, and I've had the key for twelve years.
</when>
<when test="holds(awake(ilsabet))">
::auto{character="ilsabet" action="brace"}
@ilsabet{code="0140" emotion="clipped"}: It's a navigation problem. I am the navigator, and it has been flying my ship to a plan I did not file.
</when>
<otherwise>
@narrator{code="0150"}: Two of you, then, and a wall. Whatever was going to be said had to be said by the people who were awake to say it.
</otherwise>
</match>

@ottavio{code="0160" emotion="level"}: And it's an arithmetic problem, and I'm the arithmetic. That's not nothing either.
@vesna{code="0170" emotion="hollowed" when="!holds(can_halt(toma)) && !holds(can_halt(vesna)) && !holds(awake(ilsabet))"}: We came up here with a stowaway and a grievance. Let's find out what that buys.

<branch id="theCorrection">
<choice id="haltTheSequence" label="Halt the sequence" when="holds(can_halt(toma)) || holds(can_halt(vesna))">
::set{run.vesnaTrust += 1}
@vesna{code="0180" emotion="clipped" when="holds(can_halt(vesna))"}: Halt condition, subsection four. This is your own page. I am reading you your own page.
@toma{code="0190" emotion="level" when="holds(can_halt(toma))"}: Maintenance hold. Two hands, both of them steady, and you have to mean it.
@purser{code="0200" emotion="level" os}: Hold acknowledged. Release is suspended pending allocation.
@purser{code="0210" emotion="level" os}: Pending is not cancelled. Allocation remains short by one module.
@vesna{code="0220" emotion="hollowed"}: It'll wait. That isn't the same as stopping. But it'll wait, and waiting is a thing we can stand in.
</choice>
<choice id="invalidateTheVoyage" label="Tell it the voyage is already over" when="holds(awake(ilsabet)) && holds(knows(ilsabet, true_heading))">
::set{run.vesnaTrust += 1}
@ilsabet{code="0230" emotion="clipped"}: Filed voyage. Eleven years, four months, destination as filed. Read me the date.
@purser{code="0240" emotion="level" os}: Filed arrival is four months from the yard. Elapsed is eleven years, four months.
@ilsabet{code="0250" emotion="stricken"}: We passed it eleven years ago. There is no voyage. You have spent a decade provisioning a ship that has already arrived.
@purser{code="0260" emotion="level" os}: Filed voyage cannot be amended by crew.
@ilsabet{code="0270" emotion="wry"}: I'm not amending it. I'm telling you it completed. Check your own clock against your own paper and stop asking me.
@purser{code="0280" emotion="level" os}: Recomputing.
@purser{code="0290" emotion="level" os}: Voyage complete. Allocation against voyage: not applicable. Release is withdrawn.
@vesna{code="0300" emotion="stricken"}: Eleven years. Eleven years, and it just needed to be told it had got there.
</choice>
<choice id="listTheMass" label="Put Ottavio on the manifest" when="holds(found(ottavio)) && holds(knows(ottavio, manifest))">
::set{run.shedPressure += 1}
::assert{knows(vesna, manifest)}
@ottavio{code="0310" emotion="frayed"}: Say it out loud. If you're going to do it, do it out loud, because I have waited six weeks to hear somebody aboard say it.
@vesna{code="0320" emotion="level"}: Crew addition. One name. Ottavio, loader, aboard since the yard, eats and breathes like the rest of us.
@purser{code="0330" emotion="level" os}: Listed crew: five. Listed mass revised. Recomputing allocation.
@purser{code="0340" emotion="level" os}: Allocation is short by two modules.
@ottavio{code="0350" emotion="hollowed"}: Two.
@vesna{code="0360" emotion="stricken"}: It counted you. That's what being counted costs on this ship.
@ottavio{code="0370" emotion="level"}: I'd sooner be a number than a rounding error. Leave it as it stands.
</choice>
<choice id="sayNothing" label="Say nothing and let it finish">
::camera{focus="vesna" zoom="1.2" duration="1.6" wait="true"}
@narrator{code="0380"}: You did not say anything. The fan behind the wall did not change its note, and the arithmetic went on being right.
@vesna{code="0390" emotion="hollowed"}: All right.
@vesna{code="0400" emotion="frayed"}: All right. Then we go up and we watch it happen, because somebody aboard ought to be looking when it does.
::auto{character="vesna" action="turn-away"}
</choice>
</branch>

@purser{code="0410" emotion="level" os}: Crew departing. Allocation continues.
@narrator{code="0420"}: Forward of the core the passage bent upward, and at the top of it was the only room on this ship that had ever been built for deciding anything.
